Define / choose the used models for the evaluation
    Questions to ask:
        1. is the actual code / implementation publically available
            If yes, implement exactly as is. Otherwise, take the architecture and build from scratch

 Used Models:

 1. (Classic DL - ConvNets) TinyLidarNet (1D ConvNet) (2024)
    Input: Raw 1D Lidar Data (270° Field of View)
    Output: Steering Angle + velocity
    Use Case: Autonomous Racing

 2. (Unsupervised NN-free ML) DBSCAN Clustering (2023)
    Input: Lidar Scan + Cartesian Point Cloud + History of Scans 
    Output: Line segments (obstacles on the path to the goal)
    Use Case: indoor robot navigation

3. (RL + DNN) Deep Q-Learning + GRU by Kim et al. (2020)
    Input: Lidar Map (robot state) + Robot-Goal Relationship
    Output: Q-Values for all possible actions with Post-Processing to Angular Velocity
    Use Case: Autonomous Car Parking in outdoor parking lots
4. (Supervised NN-free ML) Decision tree (imitation learning) (2021)
    Input: Lidar Map + Goal Information + History
    Output: Concrete navigation command (action to take)
    Use Case: Robot Navigation in indoor environments with obstacles on the way

Non-used models:

1. (DNN-based) ConvNet + Skip Connections by Wang et al. (2017)
    Input: Lidar Scan + Goal information
    Output: Angular rate + Velocity of a robot
    Use Case: Simulated car navigation in open scenarios with obstacles 
4. (Supervised NN-free) Fuzzy Logic and iterative decision trees by Hamzei et al. (1998)
    Input: Lidar Map + Goal Information
    Output: Angular Rate + Velocity
    Use Case: Simulated navigation in static spaces with local sensing only
5. (Supervised NN-free) Support Vector Machines (2021)
    Input: 3D Lidar data
    Output: Object class identified
    Use Case: Autonomous Driving
6. (Supervised NN-free) Particle Filter + Kalman Filter (2019)
    Input: 2D Lidar scan + orientation changes of robot + distance traveled + environment parameters
    Output: Lateral deviation + angular deviation
    Use Case: outdoor robot navigation on the wineyards within the rebstöcke
7. (Unsupervised NN-free) PEARL (2018)
    Input: 2D lidar map
    Output: Direction command to move + angular velocity
    Use Case: agricultural robot

